Input: {"question": "Who recorded \"The Wonder of You\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 0, "end": 72, "text": "The Wonder of You \"The Wonder of You\" is a song written by Baker Knight."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 73, "end": 169, "text": "It was originally recorded by Vince Edwards in 1958, but this recording has never been released."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 170, "end": 216, "text": "In 1959, Ray Peterson released it as a single."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 217, "end": 329, "text": "The song became a Top 40 hit for him on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100, peaking at #25, and also reached #23 in the UK."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 330, "end": 378, "text": "That same year it was recorded by Ronnie Hilton."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 379, "end": 443, "text": "His version was also a hit reaching #22 on the UK Singles Chart."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 444, "end": 507, "text": "The Ray Peterson record briefly re-entered the Hot 100 in 1964."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d00", "start": 508, "end": 520, "text": "In the early"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "easy listening at its best."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 28, "end": 276, "text": "The popular trio's material is no small part of the LP's success, and includes their current single, \"The Wonder of You,\" their not to be imitated version of \"Let Go,\" the Oscar-winning \"Windmills of Your Mind,\" and the much recorded \"Yellow Days.\""}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 277, "end": 358, "text": "Credit producer Allen Stanton and arranger Nick DeCaro for a job very well done.\""}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 359, "end": 406, "text": "The album reached #194 on the Billboard charts."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 407, "end": 554, "text": "Two singles from the album made the charts: \"Let Go\" at #36 on the Billboard Adult Contemporary chart and \"Kumbaya\" at #38 on the UK singles chart."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d01", "start": 555, "end": 572, "text": "Side One Side Two"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d02", "start": 0, "end": 396, "text": "4 non consecutively, it registered, inter alia, weekly sales of 35,456, 28,590, 29,647, 32,261, 44,446, 54,011, 60,979, 73,461, 35,915, 15,983, 9,575, 3,540, 1,900, 1,300 and 1,000 thus totalling sales of 505,000 units while landing at #2, #3, #5, #5, #3, #4, #4, #3, #3, #4, #7, #17, #32, #48, #61, #70, #96, #65, #58, #79 and #89 respectively, and earning a BPI Gold and Platinum certification."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d02", "start": 397, "end": 558, "text": "It is Elvis' 13th UK number-one album, making him the solo artist with most UK number-one albums (and overall only behind The Beatles with 15 number-one albums)."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d02", "start": 559, "end": 598, "text": "Elvis also extended the record for most"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d03", "start": 0, "end": 554, "text": "In Love Elvis Presley 2:57 Return to Sender Elvis Presley 2:08 ( You 're The ) Devil in Disguise Elvis Presley 2:19 Bossa Nova Baby - Remastered Elvis Presley 2:05 Viva Las Vegas - Remastered Elvis Presley 2:23 Big Boss Man - Elvis R & B Version Elvis Presley 2:51 A Little Less Conversation Elvis Presley 2:12 If I Can Dream - Stereo Mix Elvis Presley 3:09 Memories - Stereo Mix Elvis Presley 3:05 In the Ghetto Elvis Presley 2:57 Suspicious Minds Elvis Presley 4:30 Do n't Cry Daddy - Remastered Elvis Presley 2:46 Kentucky Rain Elvis Presley 3:17 Polk"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "use the Spotify app instead ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 30, "end": 51, "text": "X You 're signed in !"}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 52, "end": 128, "text": "About the streaming player : Songs play if you keep the player window open ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 129, "end": 170, "text": "The music stops if you close the window ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 171, "end": 327, "text": "To keep the music playing while you visit other pages , two options : In top row of the player , click Pop-Up Player button to open player in a new window ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 328, "end": 363, "text": "Keep player open in a browser tab ."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 364, "end": 401, "text": "Visit other pages in a separate tab ."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d04", "start": 402, "end": 476, "text": "X We 're sorry , this service does n't work with Spotify on mobile devices"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d05", "start": 0, "end": 167, "text": "is not to say that he ’ d lost it completely– “ Suspicious Minds ” shows he could still perform credibly , even if not with the panache he still had a decade earlier ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d05", "start": 168, "end": 240, "text": "So I wonder what RCA was thinking in releasing such an uninspired disc ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d05", "start": 241, "end": 448, "text": "Could it be they perceived the vacuum the Beatles left behind them was so huge–and that Elvis really was so miraculous in his “ comeback ” –that just about anything touched by the hand of The King would do ?"}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d05", "start": 449, "end": 501, "text": "People have been known to believe crazier things… .."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0483-fcad1a677e7e:d05", "start": 502, "end": 509, "text": "0 Reply"}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Vince Edwards", "Ray Peterson", "Ronnie Hilton", "Elvis Presley", "Baker Knight"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Vince Edwards", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Ray Peterson", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Ronnie Hilton", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "Elvis Presley", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R4", "answer": "Baker Knight", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
